lib\utils\accounts\account_manager\README.md:34:## Cookie Manager
lib\utils\accounts\account_manager\README.md:36:`CookieManager` Interceptor can help us manage the request/response cookies automatically.
lib\utils\accounts\account_manager\README.md:37:`CookieManager` depends on the `cookie_jar` package:
lib\utils\accounts\account_manager\README.md:39:> The dio_cookie_manager manage API is based on the withdrawn
lib\utils\accounts\account_manager\README.md:40:> [cookie_jar](https://github.com/flutterchina/cookie_jar).
lib\utils\accounts\account_manager\README.md:42:You can create a `CookieJar` or `PersistCookieJar` to manage cookies automatically,
lib\utils\accounts\account_manager\README.md:43:and dio use the `CookieJar` by default, which saves the cookies **in RAM**.
lib\utils\accounts\account_manager\README.md:44:If you want to persists cookies, you can use the `PersistCookieJar` class, for example:
lib\utils\accounts\account_manager\README.md:47:dio.interceptors.add(CookieManager(PersistCookieJar()))
lib\utils\accounts\account_manager\README.md:50:`PersistCookieJar` persists the cookies in files,
lib\utils\accounts\account_manager\README.md:51:so if the application exit, the cookies always exist unless call `delete` explicitly.
lib\utils\accounts\account_manager\README.md:53:> Note: In flutter, the path passed to `PersistCookieJar` must be valid (exists in phones and with write access).
